## 4. DATASET — CICIDS2017

### 4.1 Why CICIDS2017?

| Criterion | CICIDS2017 | NSL-KDD | UNSW-NB15 |
|-----------|-----------|---------|-----------|
| **Year** | 2017 | 2009 (original 1999) | 2015 |
| **Realism** | Real network with modern attacks | Synthetic, outdated attack profiles | Semi-synthetic |
| **Attack types** | 7 modern categories | 4 generic categories | 9 categories |
| **Labeling** | Per-flow, per-attack-type | Binary only | Multi-class |
| **Features** | 80+ flow-level features | 41 features | 49 features |
| **Community adoption** | Most-cited IDS dataset (5000+ papers) | Legacy standard | Growing |

### 4.2 Attack Types Trained On (7 categories)

| Attack | Training Samples | Detection Rate |
|--------|-----------------|----------------|
| **DDoS** | 128K+ flows | 99.98% recall |
| **DoS** | 193K+ flows | 99.89% recall |
| **PortScan** | 1.9K flows | 98.72% recall |
| **BruteForce** | 9.1K flows | 99.81% recall |
| **WebAttack** | 2.1K flows | 98.79% recall |
| **Botnet** | 1.4K flows | 91.23% recall |
| **Infiltration** | 36 flows | 91.67% recall (low precision due to tiny sample) |

### 4.3 Balanced Sampling

- **Problem:** DDoS has 128K samples vs Botnet's 1.4K — model would be biased toward DDoS.
- **Solution:** Cap each class at 50,000 samples during training. Use `class_weight="balanced"`.
- **Train/Test split:** 75/25 with stratification.

### 4.4 Cross-Dataset Validation (CIC-IDS2018)

- **Result:** RF accuracy dropped to ~50% on IDS2018 data.
- **Why:** IDS2018 uses different feature schemas, different attack tools, and different network topologies.
- **Honest answer for defense:** "The model generalizes well within the CICIDS2017 feature space but requires retraining for different network environments. This is expected for supervised ML in cybersecurity — attack patterns are environment-specific."

---

## 5. VALIDATION RESULTS

### 5.1 Aggregate Metrics (across 1.85M samples)

| Metric | Score |
|--------|-------|
| Accuracy | 99.5-99.98% per dataset |
| ROC-AUC | 0.986 - 1.000 |
| Weighted F1 | 0.95 - 0.999 |

### 5.2 Stress Test Results

| Test | Result |
|------|--------|
| **Zero traffic** (all zeros) | 100% classified as benign ✅ |
| **Random noise** | 0% flagged as attack ✅ |
| **Extreme values** | 0% false positives ✅ |
| **Feature concentration** | Top 5 features hold 31.4% importance — no single feature dominates |
| **Decision confidence** | 88.5% of predictions are "very confident" (>0.9 or <0.1) |

### 5.3 Top 5 Most Important Features

1. BWD PACKET LENGTH MEAN (7.86%)
2. AVG BWD SEGMENT SIZE (6.11%)
3. BWD PACKET LENGTH STD (5.96%)
4. PACKET LENGTH VARIANCE (5.86%)
5. BWD PACKET LENGTH MAX (5.63%)

